  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "If $U={-80,-75,-70,\u2026,30}$ is the universal set and $A={-80,-70,-60,\u2026,30},$ then $\\overset{\u2015}{A}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the multiples of $5$ from $-80$ through $30,$ while the set $A$ consists of the multiples of $10$ from $-80$ through $30.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the multiples of $5$ from $-75$ through $25$ that are not multiples of $10.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{A}={-75,-65,-55,\u2026,25}.\n$$",
